    "title": "pandas.DataFrame.__iter__ — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DataFrame.__iter__#\n\n- DataFrame.__iter__()[source]#\n- Iterate over info axis. For a DataFrame this yields column names (labels); for a Series it yields the single name. Enables iteration over the object with `for col in df` .\n  - Returns:\n    - iterator\n    - Info axis as iterator.\n See also \n  - `DataFrame.items`\n  - Iterate over (column name, Series) pairs.\n  - `DataFrame.itertuples`\n  - Iterate over DataFrame rows as namedtuples.\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame({\"A\": [1, 2, 3], \"B\": [4, 5, 6]}) >>> for x in df: ... print(x) A B",
    "markdown_length": 546,
